in today's video i'm gonna share with  you my 2020 holiday gift guide for dads  who love games  hard to believe but 2020 is thankfully  just about over and on the bright side  this means the holidays are right around  the corner  so for all the significant others kids  or other family members out there  looking for that perfect gift for your  video game loving dad  i've got you covered and we're starting  right now people of the international  retro record tour here for meeting for  the first time  i'm just a dad who loves games and the  stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and also stream over on twitch  it's always baffled me to hear my wife  say that it's difficult to buy me gifts  seems pretty obvious to me but hey she's  not much of a gamer and isn't really  that into tech so i guess it kind of  makes sense and that's where today's  video comes in  we'll run through 10 gaming gift ideas  for dads and honey  if you're watching and still looking for  something to get me this year i mean  just saying  a few hints here i'll be including links  to all of these products down in the  description below  if you're interested in purchasing of  course if you have any questions feel  free to let me know down in the comments  as well  this year we have the release of two  next-gen consoles in the playstation 5  and  xbox series x there's also the xbox  series  s which is a cheaper less powerful  version of the series x  the problem here is these are going to  be insanely hard to find this holiday  season  if you haven't pre-ordered already  chances are you probably won't get one  this year  there is a third option when it comes to  consoles though and that's the nintendo  switch  the switch went through quite a shortage  of its own throughout the summer when  many of us were locked down and  quarantined  it seems that nintendo has started to  catch up with demand though and you can  usually find them in stock online at  least  at the time of this recording that could  change  there are two versions of the switch  first there's the standard version which  can be used on the go or placed in the  included dock to play on your tv  there's also the nintendo switch lite  which is a handheld only version of the  system  but it's 100 cheaper both run all the  same games and there are a ton of great  ones on the nintendo switch  zelda breath of the wild mario odyssey  and smash bros are a few of my favorites  the switch is honestly a great system  even if you plan on getting a ps5 or  xbox series x at some point  there are just so many top notch  exclusive nintendo titles that you won't  be able to play  anywhere else so what about buying games  as  gifts unless you're buying a brand new  system you may  actually want to stay away from buying  games for dads  typically when you think of buying for  gamers the first item family members  think of  is a game right makes sense here's the  problem going this route though  most dads are going to purchase the main  games they want themselves  i know for games that i'm eagerly  anticipating i usually make plans to buy  at launch or perhaps i have some sort of  trade-in deal i'm taking advantage of  so if you're thinking about going with  that approach just make sure you check  in with dad first to see what games he's  already pre-ordered  also with new consoles hitting this year  it's more important than ever to make  sure you're picking the right version of  the game  a lot of the big titles this year are  releasing on four different platforms  ps4  xbox one ps5 and xbox series x  regardless of where your gamer dad likes  to play you can always check out  accessories such as extra controllers or  headsets as well  if you're looking for an extra  controller you'll mostly want to stick  with the first party options from sony  microsoft and nintendo  for ps5 sony has also made their own  media remote  headset and charging dock for the  controllers now maybe you're looking for  something that  dad can enjoy with the kids in that case  check out mario kart live circuit this  is a new i would say kind of an  experimental title from nintendo that  uses  augmented reality technology to create a  race track  out of your home now this actually does  come with a physical  cart that will move around your home so  you want to make sure that you have at  least a decent amount of space that you  can set this up in  then as you race through your house  you'll also see the action take place  on your screen lots of fun for both kids  and parents here with this one  there's also nintendo labo which has  been out for a bit now and you can  usually find it heavily discounted  labo is an interesting idea from  nintendo that has players putting  together physical cardboard items such  as a fishing pole  which then interact with games that come  bundled in the fun with nintendo labo is  the bonding time you get with your kids  during the build process i actually have  one of these kits that my son and i have  really enjoyed putting together  and then you get to see your creation  utilized in game  speaking of new tech though if the data  in your life hasn't jumped into vr yet  now could be the time as standalone  units are getting better  and more affordable every year for this  year i'd recommend the oculus quest  2 vr headset this is a standalone vr  unit meaning you don't need an expensive  gaming pc or any other  extra hardware to use it the 64 gigabyte  unit retails for 2.99  now if you're looking for something a  little bit cheaper or maybe some  stocking stuffers here then there are a  great number of  books out there on video games console  wars by blake harris is an oft  recommended title and a great place to  start  it tells the story of the 90s rivalry  between nintendo and sega which changed  the course of video games forever  there's also the ultimate history of  video games by stephen kent which is  another solid choice  this one focuses on a much broader  history of video games spanning across  multiple companies  and games if you're looking for fiction  titles instead then check out ready  player one which was made into a major  motion picture back in 2018  now if it's too hard to choose just one  book or maybe your loved one is a big  reader then you could always look into  gifting them a subscription to  audible you can even try audible  yourself with a free one month trial to  either their plus plan or premium plus  plan  just make sure you cancel before the 30  days is up if you decide not to keep the  plan  you can find the links and all the  details down in the description  moving on to our next item we have video  game themed lego  again this is another item families can  work on as a group  my son and i love tackling projects like  puzzles or lego together  there are a couple of incredible sets  available this year including both  minecraft and mario themed sets  the mario ones are some of my favorites  because you can get creative and build  your own levels by adding on expansion  sets when you're ready  now we've talked about consoles we've  talked about games we've talked about  accessories but one of the most  important  pieces of furniture for any gamer is  going to be their chair  if you're buying for someone who games  on a tv and maybe there's not much space  or you want something that's easily  stowed away  then i highly recommend video rockers  honestly it looks like these are made  for  kids but i actually find them super  comfortable as well i'd stay away from  the more expensive ones which have like  these audio features that  you probably won't end up using and  instead focusing on something more basic  but comfortable now if you prefer to  keep the gifts coming all year long then  you may want to check out  loot crate and their loot gaming  subscription box you can gift your loved  one a 1 month  6 month or 12 month subscription now if  you're not familiar with loot crate how  it works is they send out a crate to you  each month that includes four to six  items valued at a minimum  of sixty dollars the crates may include  collectibles apparel figures and more  part of the fun is the surprise you get  when seeing the new crate arrive each  month  if you happen to be shopping for kids  this year be sure and check out my  other video featuring my top 10 nintendo  switch games for kids  as always thank you so much for watching  i'll talk to you again soon
 

